Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SLOTS=2 and EDEN_UP_AHEAD_TWO: two frames in flight, each guarded; off by default

GrowingBlackBeans ran two frames in flight on a base PS5 (12 Nov, his 0924,
EDEN_GBB_FRAMES_AHEAD2, three runs a side): walking 23.1 -> 25.2 fps, slowest 1%
75 -> 57 ms, the present's wait 11-16 ms -> under 1 ms. It flickered, because the copy
guard (0491-0504) holds one frame: a present that finds it still up for the frame before
only counts an overlap and leaves its own frame unguarded (9-15% of his presents).

EDEN_UP_AHEAD_TWO=1 (with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1): a present waits for the frame two
back instead of the previous one, and never for its own.

EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_SLOTS=2 (with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=1/2/3): the guard has a slot per
frame in flight, with its own pages, trap and fence. A copy belongs to the slots that
needed it when it was taken, so a page may have two (one for the older frame, made before
the newer frame's present, and one made after it), and a write to a page both frames read
takes one copy for both. The back records frames in order and runs ahead of the fences, so
a read takes the copy of the frame the back records (BackPassed, run in order after each
present's lists), failing that a newer guarded frame's copy (older than memory). With two
slots a frame's read pages end when the back passes it, not at its fence: ended at the
fence they mixed the next frames' reads in and the guess for the next guard missed pages
(host stress test: 3-4% of reads wrong before, 0 after). What uploads read from a frame's
copies goes back to the next gather once the back has passed it, and =3 holds a write only
until the back has passed the newest frame guarded when it was made. A present also lifts
a slot whose fence is reached but whose fence action has not run yet. A slot is lifted at
its own fence; a writer that gives up waiting lifts the slots it waited for.

Unset (one slot): as before. The log line per 300 presents adds slots and arms made beside
another; the copies line adds copies shared by both slots and reads that took a newer
frame's copy. Neither switch is in the shader-store stamp.

Host tests (tools/experiments/ahead-guard-slots): unit cases for both slot counts and a
full pool, and a threaded stress (game, back and fence threads, 400 frames, two in
flight): two slots 0 wrong reads in 5 runs; one slot ~65% wrong (the control).

Not covered, as before: texture data and descriptor tables the texture cache reads.

